        <dataSetInformation>
            <common:UUID>37c060d3-7997-3b82-8484-cc4231514484</common:UUID>
            <name>
                <baseName xml:lang="en">Uranium enrichment centrifuge plant</baseName>
            </name>
            <classificationInformation>
                <common:classification>
                    <common:class level="0" classId="e70d2ea9-becd-32e6-9944-c946e949f129">fuels</common:class>
                    <common:class level="1" classId="d9d22a1b-abde-33c5-a1bd-13c677d7ad0e">uranium</common:class>
                    <common:class level="2" classId="12eebfcf-f3b0-3e43-8621-e24a1b053a00">enriched</common:class>
                    <common:class level="3" classId="697dc0d1-c059-39d7-a044-f3060403e330">infrastructure</common:class>
                </common:classification>
            </classificationInformation>
            <common:generalComment xml:lang="en">The material and energy requirements for construction have been roughly estimated on the basis of the data from an old US reference and scaling them down by the ratio of the capacities (centrifuge process is modular, therefore in first approximation linearity can be assumed for requirements). It is assumed that 75% of reinforced concrete is dumped as non-contaminated waste from decommissioning. Transport requirements recalculated either using ecoinvent standard distances for Europe (e.g. for chemicals) or given average distances by train from Chinese 2004 statistics or own assumptions. This dataset has been developed with the goal to serve a preliminary estimation of the Chinese nuclear chain for the Chinese electricity mix. Hence, it cannot be used for comparisons of centrifuge enrichment infrastrucure among countries.;
UUID: 37c060d3-7997-3b82-8484-cc4231514484</common:generalComment>
        </dataSetInformation>
